<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Middle Angles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a> were a group of Anglian peoples in the east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, around the Fens and the Nene and Welland valleys. Around 653 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a> made his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peada">Peada</a> their ruler, and Peada's baptism brought the first Christian mission to Mercian territory. They were later absorbed into Mercia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/middle-angles.jpg" alt="Middle Angles" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amitchell125 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anglo-Saxon_England_2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
